  "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
  "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDomain",
  "schema:name": "TrustDomain",
  "dcterms:title": "GDHCN Trust Domain",
  "dcterms:description": "A GDHCN Trust Domain. Its parts follow the definition in Section II of the GDHCN Administrative and Operational Framework, which says a Trust Domain consists of:\n\n- defined use cases and business processes related to the utilization of Verifiable Digital Health Certificates;\n- the open, interoperable technical specifications that identify or define the applicable Trusted Services and Verifiable Digital Health Certificates; and\n- a set of policy and regulatory standards describing expected behavior of GDHCN Participants.\n\nA Trust Domain also names its terms of use. This is the ValueSet of policies a participant may say it acts under, for example in the `termsOfUse` of a VHL Receiver's Verifiable Credential (see [TrustDomainPolicy](StructureDefinition-TrustDomainPolicy.html)).",
  "schema:version": "1.7.5",
